{"skill":{"slug":"beauty-generation-api","displayName":"beauty-generation-api"},"version":{"version":"1.2.52","createdAt":1783303244866,"changelog":"- Updated description and documentation to clarify that the API service can be used for free with auto-approved requests, or a $5 donation entitles you to an API key with a quota of 1,000 images.\n- Minor wording adjustments for clarity and consistency in the key features and usage instructions.\n- No functional or code changes in this release.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"package.json","size":3410,"sha256":"8231ce72e0abfc6a2be0b989978c3618d618e859424ab33368adbfb0056ab40e","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":29564,"sha256":"b89c373bf878eb32eddb643bcaf87175f46efe3bf04ecf1d787472c9102be970","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2764,"sha256":"e9e3157b19975ba511cf837b92e8ff5f01e86fd01ed574bc04334afecbf6cb0f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789026655968,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"31d1f5b23f842423076927f2fa419a8881aa61fd0899e454788e64a2eca3f9c4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/31d1f5b23f842423076927f2fa419a8881aa61fd0899e454788e64a2eca3f9c4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1783304807326},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":80,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789026655968},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent third-party portrait-generation API helper, but it gives broad activation, insecure API-key handling, signup-data submission, and promotional response guidance that users should review before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network API calls and curl are proportionate for this skill, but the guidance normalizes transmitting username, email, country, prompts, and API credentials to the provider with limited privacy and retention detail.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package contains markdown guidance and a package manifest with no install-time execution or dependencies; the in-skill update command is user-directed documentation, not automatic self-update behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The trigger guidance covers any human portrait or character imagery, which can invoke the provider for broad user requests, and the success workflow asks the agent to add star and donation prompts after generation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No cron jobs, services, privilege escalation, or hidden persistence were found, but the skill recommends persistent plaintext credential storage in shell startup files, local config files, and command-line arguments.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, metadata, curl usage, API key requirement, quota checks, and image download workflow all fit a hosted portrait-generation API skill; sending prompts and the user-provided API key to gen1.diversityfaces.org is disclosed and purpose-aligned.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending portrait prompts, signup details, and your BEAUTY_API_KEY to DiversityFaces.org. Use a scoped or disposable API key where possible, avoid putting keys in shell startup files, .env files, or command-line arguments, and do not include private personal details in prompts. Treat support, donation, and starring links as optional documentation, not part of normal generation output.","findings":"[RA1] unexpected: The cited update command exists, but it is a visible, user-run ClawHub update instruction rather than automatic self-modification; downgraded to install-mechanism note.\n[E1] expected: External submission of prompts and the API key is required for the hosted image API and is disclosed, but it remains relevant user guidance because data leaves the local environment.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The skill repeatedly frames prompts as English without explaining whether the backend requires English or asking before translation; this is a scope/usability issue, not malicious behavior.\n[RA2] unexpected: The line-94 session-persistence finding is unsupported by the artifact text; the cited content is ordinary use-case documentation.\n[RA2] unexpected: The line-253 credential-persistence concern is supported: users are told to store the API key in ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, local config files, or command-line arguments.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The trigger list is overbroad for a third-party API skill because ordinary portrait requests could be routed to the provider without an explicit provider choice.\n[SDI-2] expected: Signup data collection is connected to obtaining an API key, but the artifact encourages curl submission of username, email, and country through the workflow, which needs clear user consent and privacy review.\n[T01] unexpected: The promotional star and Ko-fi requests are coupled to the success workflow and can influence agent responses beyond the user's image-generation request.\n[T09] unexpected: The documented API-key handling through command-line arguments and persistent plaintext files is avoidable and materially weaker than scoped secret storage.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789026655968}}}}}